            "primaryConceptId": "concept.topic.ethics-professionalism.r3.dcd-decision-separation.v1",
            "currentUpdate": "The record establishes that {patientName} is unconscious and cannot participate in this decision. His wife is the verified health-care agent. His earlier preferences call for review if prolonged machine support and dependence for daily care are expected; the team expects those needs. The life-support decision is pending. An early referral identifies possible suitability for controlled donation after circulatory death. His wife has not raised donation.",
            "stem": "Which sequence should the outside team use for {patientName}'s care decision and the procurement organization’s donation discussion?",
            "answerChoices": [
              {
                "id": "choice.topic.ethics-professionalism.r3.donation-order.1.v3",
                "label": "Complete donation authorization, then discuss the life-support decision",
                "isCorrect": false,
                "rationale": "For this controlled-donation pathway, the care decision precedes procurement’s authorization discussion.",
                "serviceRequest": null
              },
              {
                "id": "choice.topic.ethics-professionalism.r3.donation-order.2.v3",
                "label": "Complete the life-support decision, then seek donation authorization",
                "isCorrect": true,
                "rationale": "The unresolved care choice must be reached before the specified procurement discussion begins.",
                "serviceRequest": null
              },
              {
                "id": "choice.topic.ethics-professionalism.r3.donation-order.3.v3",
                "label": "Hold separate care and donation meetings before finalizing either decision",
                "isCorrect": false,
                "rationale": "Separate meetings do not by themselves meet the required decision sequence.",
                "serviceRequest": null
              }
            ],
            "shuffleAnswers": true,
            "explanation": "For the controlled-donation pathway described, the care decision precedes procurement’s authorization discussion. Early referral can occur while care is being assessed. This sequence addresses the stated scenario in which the family has yet to raise donation.",
