            "primaryConceptId": "concept.ostomy-enterocutaneous-fistula.intermittent-obstruction.v1",
            "currentUpdate": "Outside clinic record. Despite prescribed loperamide, {patientName} had bouts of cramping and abdominal swelling while the pouch remained empty, followed by a large liquid discharge and relief. Between bouts, effluent remained substantial. At the recorded visit she was comfortable, her abdomen was soft, and stool was passing.",
