        "learningSummary": "Signal differences must be interpreted against how the images were acquired. A bright native T1 region and a postcontrast image with a different suppression setting cannot simply be compared as if contrast were their only difference. Comparable before/after acquisitions can clarify enhancement for the later planning report. Choose image-guided core sampling through the anterior approach. Both targets enhance; the stronger enhancement and shorter medial route do not outweigh tract planning. The biopsy tract, including its skin entry, must be removable with the definitive specimen. The stated anterior resection includes that tract; staying in the tumor-bearing compartment by itself would not establish this. Feasible core sampling is the preferred initial method; selected cases may require open biopsy."
